.TH MKSPREAD 1 "2026" "mkspread" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkspread \- a terminal spreadsheet with the menus and keystrokes of the classic DOS spreadsheets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkspread
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkspread
is a spreadsheet for the terminal.  It looks and works like the Release 2 DOS
spreadsheets: the \fB/\fR menu, the same keystrokes, formulas, @functions, macros
and the \fB.WK1\fR and \fB.WKS\fR file formats.  Press \fBF1\fR for help.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start with a sample worksheet.
.TP
.B \-\-expand
Use the whole terminal instead of 80x25.
.TP
.BI \-\-autosave= N
Save the worksheet to its file every \fIN\fR minutes when it has changed (0 = off).
.TP
.B \-\-keytest
Show how the terminal's keys are received.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and licence.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage text.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkspread/mkspread.conf
Settings: \fBautosave\fR (minutes), \fBrecovery\fR (seconds), \fBexpand\fR (yes/no).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mkspread/recover/
While a worksheet has unsaved changes a copy is kept here; if the program or the
terminal dies, the next start offers to recover it.  A normal exit removes it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MKSPREAD_PRINT_COMMAND
The command that receives printed text (default \fBlp\fR).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME
Where the configuration and recovery files live.
